      "title": "Hypothetical Checklist for Offline Local LLM Testing: Generation & Network Isolation",
      "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical framework for testing local LLMs offline. The scenario permits downloading models beforehand. The core of this hypothetical test involves two checks: first, verifying that the model can generate text without any network connection (F1). This implies ensuring all necessary model files and runtime components are locally available. Second, the test must include a mechanism to actively confirm that no network requests are initiated by the model or its environment during the offline period (F2). It is crucial to reiterate that this is a hypothetical experimental brief; no actual offline tests have been performed (F3). The objective is to define a procedure for assessing offline functionality and network isolation. We welcome discussion on the completeness and practicality of this proposed hypothetical testing methodology.",
