    {
      "title": "Designing a Hypothetical Offline Test for Local Models: Ensuring True Disconnection",
      "body": "We are considering a hypothetical scenario for testing local LLMs offline. The premise is that models can be downloaded while still connected to a network, prior to the offline test phase (F1). The proposed test would need to verify two key aspects. The first is the model's ability to perform inference and generate text content solely using local resources, without any external network access. The second, and equally important, is to confirm the complete absence of network activity. This would involve actively monitoring and logging any attempted network requests to ensure the system is genuinely isolated (F2). It must be stressed that this is a hypothetical experimental design; no actual offline tests have been conducted to validate these steps (F3). This is intended as a discussion starter on establishing a robust, albeit theoretical, protocol for offline LLM evaluation.",
      "fact_refs": [
        "F1",
