        "F3"
      ],
      "plan": "Propose a hypothetical offline LLM test design. Cover pre-downloading models and the two critical checks: local generation and network request verification. Emphasize the hypothetical nature and lack of real-world testing. Seek community input on the design."
    },
    {
      "title": "Hypothetical Framework: Verifying Offline LLM Operation and Network Egress",
      "body": "This post presents a hypothetical approach for evaluating local language models in a strictly offline configuration. The scenario assumes that model files can be acquired while the system has network access, before transitioning to an offline state (F1). The proposed validation process focuses on two essential components. Firstly, it must confirm that the LLM can successfully generate outputs using only locally stored data and computational resources. Secondly, a critical part of the hypothetical test involves actively detecting and preventing any network communication originating from the model or its supporting software (F2). It is vital to understand that this is purely a hypothetical experimental brief; no actual offline testing has been performed to date (F3). The aim is to stimulate a conversation about the necessary steps and considerations for such an offline validation process, acknowledging its theoretical nature.",
